# Allow-list: send Docker only what the lab build needs. target/ alone is hundreds of GB, and
# .claude/worktrees holds whole copies of the repo. A <Dockerfile>.dockerignore beside the
# Dockerfile wins over the context root's .dockerignore:
# https://docs.docker.com/build/concepts/context/#filename-and-location
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!crates/
!relay/
# cargo loads every workspace member's manifest, so the desktop crate comes along (never built).
!apps/desktop/src-tauri/
!deploy/lab/
# Files the crates pull in from outside crates/: include_str!/include_bytes!, and the build
# scripts' shared `#[path = "../../build-support/buildinfo.rs"]`.
!build-support/
!corpus/
!skills/
!specs/
!deploy/launchd/
!deploy/systemd/
**/target
**/.txtodo
**/*.cdx.json
apps/desktop/src-tauri/gen
crates/txtodo-core/fuzz
